git commit -m "Manual mapper: the AI source/field selections now use a proper filterable pick-list modal, not a browser prompt. A reusable picker (filter box on top, scrollable list, single- or multi-select with checkboxes and a Use N button) replaces every window.prompt for choosing columns: '1 source -> many fields' opens a single-select source picker; 'many sources -> 1 field' opens a single-select destination-field picker then a multi-select source picker; the per-row +AI opens a multi-select source picker pre-checked with whatever is already in the cell. All fed by the client's known source columns. The row source box keeps its inline datalist for quick single picks. Only the override REASON stays a text prompt (it is free text, not a list). Prev commit content retained: filterable source pick-list instead of typing, plus a visible many-sources-to-one-field button. New /manual-map/sources returns every legacy source column already known for the client - from all datasets its projects uploaded plus every source any learning holds - and the grid's source boxes are now a filterable combobox (HTML datalist) over that set, so the analyst picks a real column and it narrows as they type rather than typing from memory. Override no longer prompts for the source (it is chosen from the row's list); it only captures the mandatory reason. Added a toolbar 'many sources -> 1 field' button beside '1 source -> many fields' (the per-row +AI still exists) so both directions are discoverable; it asks for the destination field then runs the AI combine. Prev commit content retained: explicit per-field Override (reason mandatory) and AI-prompted one-to-many / many-to-one. Every row now has an Override... action; overriding a field that is ALREADY LEARNT requires a reason (the row highlights 'changed from X - reason required' and Save is blocked until a reason is given, per-row or via the Reason box); the reason is recorded in the learning audit trail. Two AI helpers: '1 source -> many fields' takes a source column and asks the model which target fields it legitimately populates (Location -> LocationCode + LocationName), then fills those rows; a per-row '+AI' takes candidate source columns and asks which COMBINE to fill that one field and how (First + Last -> Name via CONCAT), then sets the row's comma-separated sources + rule + join separator. Backend /manual-map/suggest handles both modes. Prev commit content retained: pipe an uploaded document into the grid, and support many-to-one / one-to-many. Prefill from document: a picker lists uploaded mapping documents covering the chosen object, and Load fields fills each source input from what that document proposed (override wins), so the analyst adjusts the doc's mapping by hand instead of a blank grid; a Document column also shows the doc's source with a click-to-use. MANY sources to ONE field: type comma-separated source columns (e.g. 'First Name, Last Name') and it saves as a CONCAT learning (all columns + a chosen join separator); the grid flags 'combines N columns' live and reloads a CONCAT with every column shown. ONE source to MANY fields already works - type the same source into each destination row. Verified the CONCAT round-trips through the real engine (First Name + Last Name -> 'Ada Lovelace'). Backend: context accepts proposal_id and returns doc_source per field; save parses multi-source into CONCAT rule_config(columns, separator) with original_value = first column so the output source-exists gate still passes. Statically verified; needs a live click-through.

Manual template mapper added to Mapping Documents (Map manually tab). Pick a client and an FBDI template and every target field of that template loads, each PRE-FILLED with its current learnt source and any previous-gold source, so the analyst edits from a starting point not a blank grid. Type a source column per field with an optional transform rule; 'Check mappings' runs the deterministic semantic guard (implausible pairs flagged inline, e.g. an identifier into a phone field) with an optional 'include AI' box for a written verdict. Save upserts client-scoped column_mapping learnings with an optional reason in the audit trail, and force-reapplies them onto that client's existing conversions so live work updates too. Backend: new /api/manual-map router with context (fields + learnt + gold), vet (guard + optional AI), and save (upsert/clear + rollout). No dataset needed - it maps at the template/library level. Statically verified; needs a live click-through.

Mapping Documents review rebuilt into a proper mapping surface using every tool. Rows now show Source arrow Destination with the object and FBDI sheet, a Learning column badging 'already learnt' with captured_from so a learnt field is never re-asked, a Previous-gold column cross-referencing what the last gold output used for that field, an AI-review column (verdict plus which of document/library it recommends, with reason), the conflict explanation, and per-row Approve/Reject plus Override. Override requires a MANDATORY reason and, on apply, writes the overridden source with 'manual override: <reason>' into the learning audit trail. New master 'Vet with AI' button runs one batched model pass over the conflict/new rows and STORES the verdict on the proposal so a return visit shows it without re-spending tokens. Full CSV export of every column (object, source, alternatives, status, learnt+from, currently-mapped, gold, AI verdict/recommends/reason, conflict, override+reason, decision, rule, system, notes). Backend: ProposedMapping gains is_learnt/learnt_from/gold_source/ai_verdict/ai_recommends/override fields; _classify adds the gold cross-reference and learnt flag; apply_proposal honours the override source+reason; new /vet and /override endpoints (override 400s without a reason). All statically verified; needs a live click-through.

AI verdicts now persist per project and never re-charge. New CandidateVerdict collection stores each (conversion, target field, source column) verdict + reason; mapping-candidates attaches them on every load and sorts wrong/unlikely to the bottom, so returning to a project shows the AI reasons with no click and no tokens. The vet endpoint skips pairs that already have a stored verdict (force to re-run), so repeat clicks cost nothing and the response reports reused + already_done. UI reflects this: the toolbar button turns into a green 'AI review done' with an already-done message on load, the per-field Vet-with-AI turns green 'AI review done' and short-circuits with 'already reviewed' instead of spending tokens, and re-running only vets newly-added options. Carries the prior shared-cache work so toolbar and detail panel stay in sync in-session. Destination-side alternatives still a follow-up. Lifted a shared aiVerdicts cache to MappingReviewPage keyed target_field_id then source_column; the toolbar vet publishes into it, and the Alternative source columns panel reads it on open, folding the verdicts in and re-sorting so a field the toolbar already vetted shows its AI reasons with zero extra tokens. If the toolbar was not run, each field still has its own Vet-with-AI button that vets only that field and writes back to the same cache. Prior layer kept: the panel already honours the deterministic guard (implausible options struck through and demoted) before any AI. Destination-side alternatives still a follow-up. The Alternative source columns panel in the inspector fetched its own candidates and never saw the toolbar vet, so its recommendations stayed unranked. It now honours the semantic guard (implausible options struck through, flagged, demoted, with the caution shown) even before AI, and has its own 'Vet with AI' button that reviews just that one field (only_uncertain false, so every option gets a verdict - cheap for one field), folds the verdicts in, re-sorts wrong/unlikely to the bottom, and shows the AI reason. So opening a field and clicking Vet updates that field's recommendations in place. Destination-side alternatives (rank target fields for a clicked source) is a separate reverse-ranking feature not yet built - flagged for follow-up. Also carries the prior fix: Vet-options-with-AI failing on wide templates plus clean up stray files. The button failed on the 1254-field Customer template because only_uncertain matched almost every unmapped field, sending hundreds of pairs to the model in dozens of sequential batches and blowing the ~100s gateway; a POST is not auto-retried so it fell straight to unavailable. Now the AI pass is capped at 60 pairs, prioritised implausible-first then lowest-confidence, and scoped by target_field_ids to the rows on screen (the UI sends the visible ids, max 120); the client also retries once on a cold-start 502/503/504. Also removes the empty Payee and Corporation files from the earlier multi-line-commit misparse. Single-line message on purpose. Full notes in SESSION_HANDOFF.md."
